Restore original order-table insertions for all mapped game addresses

The added uintptr bounds in patches 235..265 silently discarded valid
primitives when the order table lay above 0x900000. Actual Car Select uses
OT base 0x935ff0: at pose {640,1920,592}, the original queues 98 car
primitives, whereas native queues 54, missing all 38 FT4 and six 0x1c
quads. All 171 transformed vertices (2736 bytes) match literally.
Original 0x41a6e6..0x41a6ea unconditionally reads the depth bucket and
links the primitive after its actual flag/backface tests; no address
range filter exists. Remove these extra insertion guards throughout
the face handlers, retaining the original visibility/depth calculations
and exact three-store link sequence. Do not enlarge the invented range.

